# Gate of stage engine (SYNC_PLAN.md §6.5). Format: scripts/gates/README.md.
# "Gate: 1,000 seeds per CI run with these invariants; every failing seed
# becomes a regression test." The six invariants (convergence, no lost or
# twice-applied entry, queued edits survive crashes, tampering alarms without
# a state change, no relay answer deletes data or keys, settling) are what the
# simulator asserts on every seed.
run | simulator        | the simulator at 1,000 seeds with the six invariants of §6.5 (§6.5 gate) | SIM_SEEDS=1000 cargo test --locked -p taskdeck-sync --test simulator
run | regressions      | "every failing seed becomes a regression test" (§6.5 gate) | cargo test --locked -p taskdeck-sync --test regressions
run | wasm32           | "The crate compiles for wasm32-unknown-unknown as proof it does no I/O" (§6.5) | cargo check --locked -p taskdeck-sync --target wasm32-unknown-unknown
ci  | ci-seeds         | "1,000 seeds per CI run" (§6.5 gate) | engine (ubuntu-latest, windows-latest, macos-latest)
run | spec-coverage    | every clause engine owns is cited by an engine test (§3.3) | bash scripts/spec-coverage.sh engine
run | no-unimplemented | no unimplemented!() or todo!() left in engine's paths, tests included (§3.3) | bash scripts/gate-lib.sh no-unimplemented engine
run | no-skipped-tests | no skipped or ignored test in engine's paths (§3.3) | bash scripts/gate-lib.sh no-skipped-tests engine
